WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.801
Jury selection begins

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:02.969
on Thursday in Dominion

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:03.636
Voting Systems

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:06.573
$1.6 billion defamation lawsuit

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.074
against Fox News.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.609
Will Fox settle before

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:11.745
it goes to trial on April 17?

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:13.179
And either way, will

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.280
their viewers ever hear

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.382
anything about the emails

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:17.450
and texts revealed

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.451
by those in charge

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:19.452
that the network didn't

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:21.254
believe what it was actually airing?

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:21.755
Dominion

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:22.722
is accusing the network

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:23.456
of knowingly

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.658
and repeatedly airing falsehoods

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:27.127
about its voting machines rigging

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:29.462
the 2020 election in favor of Joe Biden

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:30.397
Among those

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:31.698
who are set to take the stand,

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:32.132
the network's

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:33.800
most prominent hosts like Sean

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:34.901
Hannity and Tucker

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.136
Carlson and high ranking

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:38.304
executives, including 92 year old

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:40.407
chairman Rupert Murdoch, himself.

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:41.808
Joining me now is Leigh Levine.

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:43.676
He's a veteran First Amendment lawyer

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:44.744
who when his long career

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.813
represented both Fox and CNN,

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.915
he's argued before the Supreme Court.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:51.184
CNN's still uses his former firm,

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:53.853
and he once represented me years ago.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.622
Leigh, nice to see you again.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.057
Actual malice.

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:59.059
That's an awfully high bar

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.226
knowledge of falsity

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:02.195
or reckless disregard for the truth.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.397
But this case seems to be capable

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:06.099
of meeting it. You agree?

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.435
Absolutely.

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:11.204
I've said this from the very

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:14.140
Stronger case of actual malice

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:17.911
than this one against the media entity.

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:20.480
A lot of the deposition testimony,

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.382
the texts and the emails

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:22.916
and the behind

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:24.584
the scenes has come to light

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.820
in media coverage of the pleadings.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.155
Can that be imputed

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.757
to the company at large?

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:31.858
Can the company be held

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:32.926
accountable for what

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:33.960
Tucker Carlson

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.496
may have said to a colleague?

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:37.997
Well, you know, that's the big

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.632
very interesting thing, Michael,

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.968
about the judge's decision last week

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:44.504
allowing the case to go to trial.

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:45.805
The judge basically said

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:47.907
that that's an issue for the jury,

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.275
which means that dominion

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:52.112
can put into evidence all of that stuff

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:54.914
about all of those people.

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.950
And it will be up to the jury to decide

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:58.184
whether or not

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:00.386
any of it is relevant to Fox

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:02.455
as an entity, state of mind.

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:03.523
With respect to knowledge.

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:04.557
It ought to be a reckless

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:05.925
disregard of the truth.

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:07.660
You know this as well. As I do.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.497
That is a tremendous boon for Dominion

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:13.133
Can the

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.734
defendant in this case, Fox News,

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.369
wrap themselves in opinion?

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:17.704
Can they sell what we were just

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:20.373
this was an item of of news interest

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.142
and we were putting someone on air

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.676
to express their opinion.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:26.613
We didn't necessarily buy into it.

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.481
They cannot the judge took

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:31.951
that argument by Fox off the table.

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:33.386
In his decision

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:34.754
that was released last week.

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:37.524
So the jury is going to be instructed

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:40.894
that Fox broadcast false statements

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:41.594
of fact

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:43.963
about Dominion that were defamatory.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.000
The only issue in this regard before

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:47.934
the jury

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.969
is whether or not Fox published it

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.104
with knowledge of falsity

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:51.738
or recklessness.

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:52.972
Regarding the truth

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:55.175
and who we were at Fox,

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:56.409
whose state of mind

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:57.377
with respect to truth

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.845
or falsity is relevant.

00:02:58.845 --> 00:02:59.479
Those are really

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:01.447
the only issues other than damages

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:02.248
that the jury is going to

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:03.449
be asked to decide.

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:06.986
If you were defending the case,

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:09.689
what would you be leading with

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:12.959
That's really tough.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:15.395
I think that I would be leading

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:18.097
with trying to

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:21.601
blow holes in the connecting dots

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.403
between the various people

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.805
who said things about Sidney Powell

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:27.273
being not Rudy

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:29.275
Giuliani being crazy or not

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:31.010
believing the truth

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:34.214
and what the line producers and the hosts

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.182
knew at the time.

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:37.417
But given the evidence

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:38.851
that's in the case,

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:39.619
it's going to be hard

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:41.321
to blow holes in that line.

00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:44.190
So if I were a defense lawyer

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:46.859
handling this case, I wouldn't

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:49.429
I would be really worrying about what

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:52.098
I could do by way of defense.

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:52.899
It sounds to me

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:54.067
like you'd be recommending

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:54.934
you'd be laying out

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.035
the pluses and minuses,

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:57.203
but perhaps recommending that

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:57.804
they settle.

00:03:58.838 --> 00:03:59.973
Yeah, I would

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:02.375
if I were asked for a recommendation,

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:03.643
I would recommend settlement.

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:04.677
I'm surprised that

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.879
the case has not settled so far.

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:08.748
I'm surprised it didn't settle before.

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:09.515
Or Fox

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:10.516
had to produce

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:12.252
all of these emails and texts

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:14.220
that have now become public.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:14.921
I'm surprised

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:17.690
they didn't settle after the briefing

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:18.891
when all of this was laid

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:19.959
out to the public.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:20.260
My

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:21.728
my only thought now is

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:23.896
if they're waiting for jury selection

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:25.798
to see what kind of jury they draw

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:27.300
and whether they feel comfortable

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.001
that they're

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:28.534
at least

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.303
a person or two on that jury

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:31.971
who might not

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:35.275
be interested in ruling against Fox.

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:37.944
That's the only thing I can think

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:38.645
That process

00:04:38.645 --> 00:04:40.113
scheduled to begin on Thursday.

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:41.381
Lee Levine, thank you so much.

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:42.815
Nice to see you.

00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:44.617
Good to see you, too. Michael, take care.

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:46.052
Checking in

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:49.989
on social media reaction What do we have

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:51.090
Fox should be required

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.092
by the jury to admit to their viewers

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:54.460
how Fox deceived them.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.261
This requirement

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:56.763
should preface the beginning

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:57.897
of every TV segment

00:04:57.897 --> 00:04:59.899
that airs on Fox hour by hour.

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:01.501
You raise citizen Jenn.

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.469
You raise a very interesting question,

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:04.370
which is,

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:04.871
you know,

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:06.572
if a tree falls in the forest,

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.141
is the Fox View viewer

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:09.642
even going to know about this?

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:10.376
The case has gotten

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:12.712
extensive publication in the media,

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:15.014
but it doesn't get discussed at all

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:16.382
on Fox News.

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:18.017
Even if the case is to resolve

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:20.253
with a big check being written,

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:21.821
which I anticipate,

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:23.790
will their viewers be any the wiser?

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.359
And by the way, in some far

00:05:26.359 --> 00:05:27.560
right media quarters,

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.595
they've not even taken the lesson

00:05:29.896 --> 00:05:30.697
from the judge

00:05:30.697 --> 00:05:32.765
who used all caps in explaining

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:35.068
that there is absolutely no basis

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:35.935
for any of that

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:37.970
which was said about dominion.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:38.871
In other words,

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:40.206
people are not learning the lesson,

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:41.341
at least yet,

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:42.875
from what has come out in this case.

